   103	3. **Merge.** One matter is one bet. Two entries are one matter only when the same outcome settles both and their answers cannot move apart.
   104	   Another year of a figure is another matter.
   142	   - **Answer:** supported, unsupported, insufficient, or no answer (a question not judged by the cutoff).
   143	   - **Cannot tell:** a split after the debate rounds, resolved in each counting by item 7.
   144	5. **Served in a draw:** at least one covering question is marked `worth` and supported, in each counting after item 7's resolution. A matter **served by a system** is served in
   145	   at least 2 of its 3 draws.
   146	6. **The quantities:** a = served only by the new system; b = served only by the old; N = all listed matters.
   147	7. **The two countings.** A split ("cannot tell" after the debate rounds) resolves to one of the marks its readers actually gave.
   148	   - **Counting 1:** the new system's cards take the most favourable mark given; the old system's cards take the least favourable.
   149	   - **Counting 2:** the reverse.
   150	   - **The order:** for the mapping, covers > does not cover; for the answer, supported > insufficient > unsupported; for worth, worth >
   151	     duplicate or trivia.
   152	   - **How a resolved mark counts:** it counts as that mark. A resolved supported or unsupported mark enters the decided denominators. A
   153	     resolved insufficient mark stays out of them, as any insufficient mark does.
   154	   - A guardrail subgroup is **exercised** only with at least 10 cards decided **without** a split. A subgroup that is not exercised cannot
   155	     breach. It blocks only a practical lead; a loss established otherwise still stands.
