   179	      the window), so the council took the cheaper, reversible course (D439): a later replacement would be a diagnostic only.
   180	11. **The verdicts, tested in this order:**
   181	    1. **Invalid:** a plant without an explicit rejection, fewer than 3 of 4 supported controls accepted, or fewer than 2 of 3 repeats marked
   182	       the same.
   183	    2. **Too small:** N < 20, or fewer than 30 distinct questions in any system-draw.
   184	    3. **Practical lead:** a − b ≥ max(3, ⌈0.15·N⌉) and a ≥ 2b under both countings, with every guardrail exercised and passing under both.
   185	    4. **Practical loss:** b − a ≥ max(3, ⌈0.15·N⌉) and b ≥ 2a under both countings (needing no guardrail exercised), or a breach in an
