  4798	  - Options: current production (recommended): "双方都不预设题目，条件相同；用冻结的标准、同一天、各跑三轮。“可评分的 7 道题”的结果单独列出。"; the seeded version with 22 preset questions ("新系统每轮天然少约 11 道公司财务指标题，几乎不可能赢"); the seven graded questions only.
  4799	  - Alex: "和现在的线上版本比 (Recommended)".
  4800	- **Decided:** D427's end-to-end comparison is the clean path against production as it now runs (no preset questions, D370),
  4801	  on the frozen ruler, the same day, three draws each; the seven graded questions (D395) are reported beside. The seeded
  4802	  comparison (D392) remains a diagnostic, not the gate. Raised by the council's read of where the path stands
  4803	  (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/kr-consensus.md`).
  4804	- **Scope:** the clean path's end-to-end acceptance (D427).
  4937	- **Decided (rules):** R1, a stop is shared where it is decided (the ladder step's and the judge's final stops and local cap refusals stop
  4938	  the shared ledger), and every actual send in a budgeted process reads it first (a stop gate on `urllib.request.urlopen`, installed by
  4939	  each entry point; a 403 no component retries); an attempt admitted before a stop may finish. R2, the draw record holds its identity (kind,
  4940	  label, ledger, options; a differing launch is refused) and the outcome class (a signal exit is a crash); the launcher is alive while it
  4941	  holds its lock, registered on the ledger (the registration is checked under the ledger's lock before the launcher takes its own lock,
  4942	  and the gate stops the ledger when a registered lock is free, so an orphaned child's next send and every other draw's are refused).
  4943	  R3, every shared language-model reservation is the agreed bound, and the ledger settles a missing, zero, negative or non-finite charge
  4944	  at the reservation. R4, the proof runs the real orchestration with a trap in every child process.
  4945	- **Decided (changes to WIRING-DESIGN.md §D, not readings of it):** (a) the one redo of Step 1, Step 2 and production is a relaunch with
  4946	  `--redo` and a required `--redo-reason` written to the record, made only when the component's output shows an eligible failure (a
  4947	  transport failure after its own retries, an answer refused or not fitting its schema); otherwise the run stops; the ladder step and the
  4948	  judge have no outer redo (the judge keeps its own inside `run_stage_b`). (b) A crash stops the whole run. `run_stage_b.py`'s inner
  4949	  path (a first folder with no outcome, then the redo folder) is unreachable through `run_fresh.py` and is not claimed to satisfy the crash
  4950	  rule on its own.
