The timing point is resolved in the draft. The exposure rules and the launcher-fix exception still need changes before D667 is recorded.

- **D431 timing — resolved in the text.** v8 requires D667 to be recorded before any paid send. The draft replaces the calendar-day rule for this comparison only and matches v8’s one-hour launch window, 72-hour send limit, and diagnostic outcome if either limit is missed. [Run plan §1.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v8.md:170) · [D667 draft](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/D667-draft.md:23)
- **Corpus exemption — partly resolved.** The leftover file exclusion is gone. An exact ID-set match can still exempt a probe or fixture that reused an entire listed corpus. Limit the exemption to verified raw copies of documented builds, and state that use in a probe or fixture still counts as exposure. [Run plan §1.2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v8.md:50) · [D665](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9411)
- **Replay exemption — the draft is wider than v8.** D667 omits v8’s conditions that the library was sealed or served as the product, that no decision cites one of its articles as a case behind a change, and that derived research still counts as exposure. Incorporate §1.2’s full rule. [D667 draft](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/D667-draft.md:9) · [Run plan §1.2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v8.md:80)
- **Launcher repair — the draft contradicts v8.** “Any fix” is out of scope in D667, but v8 allows a launcher-only repair and slice rerun. Carry that exception into D667. [D667 draft](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/D667-draft.md:44) · [Run plan §2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v8.md:243)

NOT READY: close the corpus matching loophole, carry over the full replay exemption, and preserve the slice’s launcher-only repair.
